meta {
  name: Unblock user
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/2/unblock
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Unblock a user

  Sets the account back to `status: 1`, `statusName: ACTIVE` — from BLOCKED, and also from PENDING — so it can sign in again.

  Sets `updated` to an audit stamp of who did it. No body is needed; anything sent is ignored.

  ## Auth

  Bearer token of a user whose role is `ADMIN` (send **auth/Log in** first; it stores `{{token}}`).

  ## Path parameters

  | Name | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | integer | yes | Positive integer. |

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

    {
      "message": "User unblocked",
      "data": {
        "id": 1,
        "roleId": 2,
        "genderId": 4,
        "documentTypeId": 1,
        "name": "Ada",
        "lastName": "Lovelace",
        "email": "ada@lpaecomms.test",
        "document": "PA1234567",
        "phone": "+61 400 000 000",
        "address": "1 Cavill Ave, Surfers Paradise QLD",
        "emailVerified": false,
        "session": null,
        "deletedAt": null,
        "role": {
          "id": 2,
          "name": "Customer",
          "code": "CUSTOMER"
        },
        "created": {
          "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
          "serverTime": "12:30:14",
          "unixTime": 1790476214,
          "user": 1,
          "role": "ADMIN"
        },
        "updated": {
          "client": "2026-10-21T01:00:00.000Z",
          "server": "2026-10-21T01:00:00.000Z",
          "serverDate": "2026-10-21",
          "serverTime": "11:00:00",
          "unixTime": 1792544400,
          "user": 1,
          "role": "ADMIN"
        },
        "statusName": "ACTIVE",
        "status": 1,
        "createdAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z"
      },
      "pagination": null
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  `id` is not a positive integer.

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "id",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  ### 401 Unauthorized — missing, invalid or expired token

    {
      "message": "Sign in to continue.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 403 Forbidden — the token's role is not ADMIN

    {
      "message": "You do not have permission to do this.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  ### 404 Not Found — no active user with this id

  Soft-deleted records answer 404 too.

    {
      "message": "User not found.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": []
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
